424. Longest Repeating Character Replacement

You are given a string s and an integer k. You can choose any character of the string and change it to any other uppercase English character. 
You can perform this operation at most k times.
Return the length of the longest substring containing the same letter you can get after performing the above operations.

Explanation:

Idea:
Maintain a sliding window.

maxFreq = frequency of most common character in current window.

To make all characters same:
changesNeeded = windowLength - maxFreq

Valid Window:
windowLength - maxFreq <= k

Invalid Window:
windowLength - maxFreq > k

Steps:
1. Expand r and update frequency.
2. Maintain maxFreq.
3. If window becomes invalid, move l forward.
4. Update max length.

Memory Trick:
Keep the majority character.
Change all other characters.


Code:

class Solution {
    public int characterReplacement(String s, int k) {
        int[] freq=  new int[26];

        int l=0; int r=0;
        int n = s.length();
        int maxFreq=0;
        int maxLen=0;

        while(r<n){
            
            freq[s.charAt(r)-'A']++;
            maxFreq=Math.max(maxFreq,freq[s.charAt(r)-'A']);

            while((r-l+1)-maxFreq>k){
                freq[s.charAt(l)-'A']--;
                l++;
            }
            maxLen = Math.max(maxLen,(r-l+1));
            r++;
        }
        return maxLen;
    }
}
